    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (78.26) and **Kyle Schwarber** (74.75) anchoring the offense, both bolstered by a massive 18% SP skill boost against Sugano. **Turner** remains our primary engine; his elite speed profile combined with the leadoff spot makes him a high-floor play despite the tough matchup. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** (72.28) provides the day\u2019s most reliable power upside, overcoming a significant platoon disadvantage against the lefty Abbott thanks to his elite 0.428 xwOBA. We are also leaning into **Junior Caminero** (66.67), whose favorable wind conditions and second-spot placement offset the challenges of facing Tolle, ensuring he remains a high-efficiency contributor for our Roto standing.\n\nIn the middle of the order, **Caleb Durbin** (63.00) and **Dillon Dingler** (62.05) represent our most effective leverage plays. **Durbin** is specifically being maximized for his stolen base potential despite a sub-optimal ninth-hole assignment, while **Dingler** benefits from a strong dynamic platoon edge against the lefty Cameron. The most difficult personnel decision was opting to bench **Chase Meidroth** (37.95). While he was a strong consideration against Gilbert, the optimizer ultimately flagged the matchup against a high-tier arm as a sub-floor risk, prioritizing our established starters to preserve limited game caps. \n\nManagement is keeping a close eye on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (52.12), whose score is suppressed by facing deGrom; despite the unfavorable SP skill rating, we are running him out there solely to chase his unique speed contribution in a category where we remain desperate for volume. We remain cautious of **Carson Benge** (47.25), who is currently performing as a marginal play; he is locked into the lineup only because we lack a superior alternative, and we will monitor his performance closely to see if he justifies the roster spot against Rodriguez. **Christian Yelich**, **Colt Keith**, and **Zac Veen** remain sidelined due to IL status or minor league assignments, leaving our active roster thin but tactically positioned for maximum efficiency.",
